Canadian multipliers for Ohio stations in the OH QSO Party -- the sponsor's 11
NL PE NS NB QC ON MB SK AB BC and NT, where NT is Yukon-NWT-Nu (NY4I, 2026-11-20).
Yukon (YT) and Nunavut (NU) keep their own QTH and count as the multiplier NT.
Newfoundland is not spelled LA here, and S50.DOM is included first: LA is Louisiana.
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

Nl = VO1,VO2,NL,NF,LB,LAB,^NF and Labrador
Pe = VY2,PE,PEI,^Pr. Edward Isl.
Ns = VE1,NS,^Nova Scotia
Nb = VE9,NB,^New Brunswick
Qc = VE2,QC,QUE,QU,PQ,^Quebec
On = VE3,ON,ONT,^Ontario
Mb = VE4,MB,MAN,^Manitoba
Sk = VE5,SK,SAS,SASK,^Saskatchewan
Ab = VE6,AB,ALB,ALT,^Alberta
Bc = VE7,BC,^British Columbia
Nt = VE8,NT,NW,NWT,^Yukon-NWT-Nu
Yt > Nt = VY1,YT,YK,YU
Nu > Nt = VY0,NU
